      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · A20/A21; Movement 35; Draft 3; the shared Neumann ground",
          "title": "Form returns with its source still able to answer",
          "italic": "What returns is a form capable of being changed by the world it discloses — the sequence closes in another finite act of seeing, where the other's answer remains their own.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The shared Neumann whole grounds the declared A20/A21 relation through differentiation, the image's power and transformed recognition; the composed whole gives that structuration its form–participation–alterity movement. Apollo returns to articulation — a definite image again offered, now bearing an acknowledged relation to the life it expresses and the difference it cannot appropriate. Dionysus remains effective within its communicability; Daphne remains",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "effective within that participation — another centre can answer without being pre-assigned the answer that would complete the speaker's image. Draft 3 gives the double demand: truth beyond any frame, truth encountered through this particular angle and life; a form once opened can close again, and the renewed encounter has to affect its valuation. Movement 35 receives the communicable perspective made transparent to participation, counter-perspective and context.\n\nDeclared cross-story: Daphne ↔ the Apollo/Dionysus bracket — the Ovidian whole and the philosophical composition retain distinct casts and operations; Dionysus is not an additional actor in Ovid's episode. ↳ Occurrences: the renewed finite seeing (#0, #5→0); the answer that remains the other's own (#3, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
